        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 2 codebook/README/label sources and 2 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"mood\", \"id\"), Documented = c(\"conflict\", \n\"no\"), Label = c(\"Sleep quality rating | Positive affect\", NA\n), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(\"mood\", NA), Source = c(\"codebook_b.csv | codebook.csv\", \nNA), Status = c(\"conflicting_definition\", \"unlabelled\")), row.names = 1:2, class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Conflicting or Ambiguous Definitions\n\n1 matched column has more than one codebook definition, or a definition scoped to a different experiment. These are matched to a codebook but need manual resolution before the label can be trusted.",
